# Scoped to `docker build -f Dockerfile.resource-miner` (BuildKit picks up
# <dockerfile-name>.dockerignore automatically). The Dockerfile's own COPY lines
# are an explicit allowlist already — this is defense in depth, keeping
# unrelated and sensitive content out of the build context entirely rather
# than trusting a dockerignore negation pattern to re-include the right subset.
#
# entitlement-navigator/ in particular: its gitignored private/ evidence
# boundary (raw genealogy imports, when populated locally) must never be
# reachable from a build context, even one that doesn't COPY it.
entitlement-navigator/
resource-miner/fixtures/
resource-miner/tests/
resource-miner/data/resources.jsonl
reports/
scripts/
src/
tests/
.git/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
